            <ArticleTitle>Giant right coronary artery (RCA) aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E167-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1532/HSF98.20121133</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery aneurysm (CAA) is a rare type of coronary artery disease. The angiographic incidence of the coronary artery aneurysm is reportedly between 1.5% to 4.9%, and it is more frequent in men. We have successfully carried out a simultaneous &quot;coronary bypass together with aneurysm ligation&quot; operation on a patient with coronary heart disease and an aneurysm within the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
